description:
FILED s521 (Fable, 2026-10-18 15:4x) from the s520a merge probes (review/p521/a3b-unqual.pl): perl / base 5e6e241d / s520a tip ed5223b4 = obj / class / class -- PRE-EXISTING, not s520a's (its #3397 fix deliberately keeps "`Name::` and single-segment names" as the class string; this task is the single-segment half).

REPRODUCER (perl 5.40.3):
    package Obj; sub m { 'obj' }
    package K; sub m { 'class' }
    package main;
    sub K { bless {}, 'Obj' }
    print K->m, "\n";
perl: `obj` (perlobj: a bareword followed by -> is a CLASS unless a sub of that name exists in the current package at compile time -- then it is K()->m).  PCL: `class`.

FIX SHAPE: the #3397 mechanism, one step wider -- `p-class-invocant` decides ONCE per site at load whether a sub of that name existed when perl compiled the site; for a single-segment name the sub to look for is CURRENT-PACKAGE::NAME (the site's package), and `K::->m` / `'K'->m` stay the class (probe both).  The same load-time snapshot rule as #3397 (a sub installed at run time in the same unit does not turn the site into a call).  Blast radius: every `Class->method` whose class name is also a declared sub in the calling package -- rare; corpus-diff + emission-ab before committing; the per-call price on every single-segment class call must stay what #3397 argued (one load-time constant test).

ACCEPTANCE: the reproducer = perl; the negatives (`K::->m`; a `sub K` declared AFTER the site in source order -- perl's rule is "exists at the site's compile time", so probe whether a later `sub K` is seen, and make PCL's snapshot agree), a guard row beside #3397's in Pl/t/universal-01.t, inverse-verified; corpus-diff / eab explained.  No census row known -- LOW; a filler for a brief that already touches p-class-invocant.
